    "lawCode": "Amd §6, add Art 5 §100 & §212-a, Mil L; amd §§2, 3 & 18, UDC Act; add Art 17 §250, St Fin L",
    "lawSection": "Military Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8181\n\nSPONSOR: HELMING\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the military law, in relation to the Lake Ontario-St.\nLawrence River flood prevention, response and recovery program; and to\namend the New York state urban development corporation act and the state\nfinance law, in relation to financing the Lake Ontario-St. Lawrence\nRiver flood prevention, response and recovery program\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would establish, under the direction of the Division and Naval\nAffairs, a Lake Ontario-St. Lawrence River flood prevention, response\nand recovery program, and would provide for the authorization to finance\nprojects under the program by the state urban development corporation.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nMore specifically, this bill would:\n\n1. Amend section 6, and add a new article five and a new section 212-a,\nof the military law, to establish a new Lake Ontario, St.  Lawrence\nRiver Flood Prevention, Response and Recovery Program under the direc-\ntion of the Adjutant General and the Division of Military and Naval\nAffairs;\n\n2. Amend sections 2, 3 and 18 of section 1, of the New York state urban\ndevelopment corporation act, to authorize such corporation to provide\nfinancing for projects under the Lake Ontario-St. Lawrence River flood\nprevention, response and recovery program; and\n\n3. Add a new article 17 of the state finance law, to provide that the\nprincipal and interest debt service on bonds or notes issued by the New\nYork state urban development corporation to finance projects of the Lake\nOntario-St. Lawrence River flood prevention, response and recovery\nprogram shall be paid from the state operations special emergency appro-\npriation.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nRecent, historic flooding along the Lake Ontario and St. Lawrence River\nWaterfronts have cause devastating effects to property owners, busi-\nnesses and municipalities. In 2017, New York enacted Lake Ontario and\nSt. Lawrence River Flood grant program to address the destruction from\nthe 2017 flooding. As increased water levels indicate that such flooding\ncould well be a more frequent occurrence, rather than simply a one time\nevent, the need has arisen to develop a prudent state government strate-\ngy to provide an effective and ongoing prevention, response and recovery\nprogram for the Lake Ontario and St. Lawrence River Waterfronts.\n\nThis bill seeks to enact such an effective and ongoing prevention,\nresponse and recovery program by empowering the state's Adjutant General\nand the Division of Military and Naval Affairs to develop and adminis-\ntrate such a program, and to provide effective resources for such\nprogram by means of financing through the state urban development corpo-\nration.\n\nThe Division of Military and Naval Affairs, through the National Guard,\nis expert in disaster prevention, response and recovery, and have the\nnecessary contacts with federal partners, such as the federal emergency\nmanagement agency and the army corps of engineers, to accomplish such an\neffective and meaningful flood prevention, response and recovery\nprogram. Additionally the state urban development corporation has\nfurther demonstrated a valuable expertise in the financing of critical\ninfrastructure and recovery projects, which would prove the backbone on\nany such effective program.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone Noted (appropriation presently exists in law)\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act takes effect immediately.\n",
